WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.000
Where the controller runs
decides what it inherits.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.862
On premises puts it
closest to the targets.

3
00:00:05.862 --> 00:00:10.418
Self-managed on cloud virtual machines
inherits that cloud's authorization,

4
00:00:10.418 --> 00:00:13.266
checked service by service
and region by region,

5
00:00:13.266 --> 00:00:16.825
and on an Azure virtual machine
it can use a managed identity.

6
00:00:16.825 --> 00:00:20.194
The two managed offerings aren't
FedRAMP-listed, and that,

7
00:00:20.194 --> 00:00:24.137
not their commercial regions, is
what keeps them out of the default.

8
00:00:24.137 --> 00:00:27.089
One of them also erases
job logs after thirty days,

9
00:00:27.089 --> 00:00:30.112
so you'd have to export them
to keep your audit trail.

10
00:00:30.112 --> 00:00:34.295
And wherever it runs, the traffic
to its targets crosses a boundary,

11
00:00:34.295 --> 00:00:37.413
so record each channel as
an external connection.

12
00:00:37.413 --> 00:00:39.550
Now, the settings to switch on.
